]], "output": "```console\ndiff --git a/Outline.md b/Outline.md\nindex c86fb41..027b0b4 100644\n--- a/Outline.md\n+++ b/Outline.md\n@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@\n-# Outline — what the paper says and what carries it (revision 21: P6 results, account a hypothesis; rev. 13: results of `experiment-repo`#6 applied; verdicts per claim; review #5 applied; Brief rev. 12: P6 κ* net of null cells, control C3, threshold floor; P7 analytic noise part)\n+# Outline — what the paper says and what carries it (revision 22: B₁ 0.967 group mean = 0.963 cell mean; revision 21: P6 results, account a hypothesis; rev. 13: results of `experiment-repo`#6 applied; verdicts per claim; review #5 applied; Brief rev. 12: P6 κ* net of null cells, control C3, threshold floor; P7 analytic noise part)\n \n Source: `idea-repo` Brief revision 12 (the idea, the predictions P1–P5, the study design and cell budget), the objective (`story-repo`#1) and `prior_work.md`. This page says *what to test and where it shows*, never what a result must be. Every claim below has a \"refuted if\" line; a result that triggers it changes the claim, and I take it to `idea-repo` (see \"When results do not carry it\").\n \n@@ -37,7 +37,7 @@ Additions to the cell list (A = review item): **(A1)** fine s grid {0,0.1,…,0.\n \n **C8 — Inference: does the nominal 95% CI cover? (review A6)** Coverage and width of the unit bootstrap (Bernoulli), the cluster bootstrap (cluster designs), graph-aware variance where available and the oracle-spec interval, across cells. The practitioner's question, and the bootstrap SE is already a P5 benchmark. Prediction to test, not assume: coverage degrades where leverage is large (variance understated by dependence) and where bias/SD is large (bias ignored by the interval). *Evidence*: coverage/width recorded in every cell (A6), cells with MC SE; sign-error rate likewise. *Figure 9*: coverage vs L and vs |bias|/SD across cells (two panels, nominal level marked, MC CI per point; C9 adds a coverage-vs-width panel if run), with sign-error rate in Table 3 (regime-map table: per cell group, RMSE ratio to DM, coverage, sign-error). *Refuted if*: coverage stays near 95% where L or bias/SD are large → the bootstrap is adequate and the P5 benchmark \"bootstrap SE\" is strong; report.\n \n-**C9 — An assumption-indexed extrapolation-sensitivity interval (Brief P6, rev. 11; exploratory-after-results on the existing cells, confirmatory on the shared block).** *Order of events, which the paper tells as it happened:* P5(ii) was predicted to work and failed; the non-identification argument was formulated afterwards as an explanation of the failure; P6 and P7 are the tests of that explanation, not something the pre-registration anticipated. The interval is the honest-CI form of Armstrong–Kolesár 2018/2020 (worst-case bias over a derivative-bounded class, rule-of-thumb M̂) with κ × the in-support magnitude as the relative-magnitudes logic of Rambachan–Roth 2023 (abstract only read); **not claimed as new**; what is new is its application to the extrapolation functional of exposure regressions (corner offsets c(p), degree dependence), the controls and κ*. Definition (frozen in the Brief): τ̂ ± cv_α(κB/SE)·SE_HC0, α = 0.10, B₁ = range of τ̂ over the ladder, B₂ = ½·M̂·((1−p)²+p²) with M̂ the largest |∂²/∂f²| of a global cubic in f (with z, z×f) over the observed range of f; κ grid {0.25, …, 64} all reported. *Main quantity:* **κ\\*** per mechanism × d, the smallest κ with mean coverage ≥ 0.90 (∞ if none): how much assumption each mechanism needs, **net of SE miscalibration** (HC0 undercovers with no bias at high leverage and small n): κ\\* is also computed on the zero-bias null cells (s = 0) as κ\\*₀ and reported raw and as κ\\* − κ\\*₀, and on a subset recomputed with the Monte-Carlo SD of τ̂ in place of SE_HC0; if κ\\* barely moves, the SE is not the issue. *Predictions (falsifiable)*: (1) smooth mechanisms: κ\\* ≤ 2 for the median mechanism × d, with a frozen κ̂ fixed on the original cells before the block is run; (2) threshold (d)\n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "b7b5a1f0-88ed-5122-821e-a4b5c73eadf8", "at": 1795662377.1801844, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 152217, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "figtab-repo", "actor": "figtab-repo", "execution_id": "e11940d68e37aced52a00808487b2266", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "d0bbdbc8-aad3-50dd-b178-a2989051df82", "at": 1795662377.1841104, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 152218, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "figtab-repo", "actor": "figtab-repo", "execution_id": "e11940d68e37aced52a00808487b2266", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "50256cb2-25d7-501c-8614-824047fba7da", "at": 1795662377.1859968, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 152219, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "figtab-repo", "actor": "figtab-repo", "execution_id": "e11940d68e37aced52a00808487b2266", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "f5d99c0c-80bd-5b19-b180-c83839d08ce2", "at": 1795662377.80309, "until": 1795662383.8404963, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 152223, "layer": "worker", "category": "model", "kind": "model.request", "role": "figtab-repo", "actor": "figtab-repo", "execution_id": "e11940d68e37aced52a00808487b2266", "trust": "system-confirmed", "outcome": "completed", "label": "model → completed", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "model request → completed in 3.6s (instruction ✓, activation ✓) [max_tokens 128000, output_config.effort high